Testbed

Reproducible ROS peers for the conformance gates: one container per supported distro, each able to speak every RMW Weld must interoperate with. All live checks are Go, plus one shell serial runner: testbed/live/serial.sh runs the ROS suites one step at a time to avoid cross-talk when parallel shards share a domain. The script never starts or stops the fleet; the fleet must already run. No other shell harnesses remain under testbed/.

Images

- weld-humble: ros:humble-ros-base plus rmw-cyclonedds-cpp plus rmw-zenoh-cpp
- weld-jazzy: ros:jazzy-ros-base plus rmw-cyclonedds-cpp plus rmw-zenoh-cpp
- weld-rolling: ros:rolling-ros-base plus rmw-cyclonedds-cpp plus rmw-zenoh-cpp

FastDDS ships in each base image. Dockerfiles pin nothing beyond the ROS apt snapshots.

Runtime

Each container idles on sleep infinity with host networking, so DDS multicast discovery works without extra configuration (testbed/docker-compose.yml:1-7).

  cd testbed
  docker compose build
  docker compose up -d
  docker compose ps

weld-jazzy is the canonical peer for the gates below. The Humble and Rolling images exist for manual cross-distro checks.

Live tests use docker argv with no shell. ImageEnv replicates the Jazzy setup as -e flags so ros2 runs directly as argv (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:115-123, DockerArgs at testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:218). Distro peers use the same pattern (testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:110). Context timeouts bound every docker and weld call. No timeout binary and no mktemp.

Layout

- testbed/unit/*: pure Go, no Docker. Port math, SPDP marshal and parse, SEDP shape, data path. Conformance files per area, not one file each: datapath 9, launch 9 (fixtures plus expected dumps), sedp 4, spdp 2, ports 2, cli 2, services 2, negative 2, chaos 3, bags 1. testbed/unit/launch/ is the launch-argument gate with fixtures plus expected dumps (see testbed/unit/launch/conformance_test.go:199).
- testbed/live/*: needs Docker and the already running weld-jazzy peer. Go entrypoint with docker argv and no shell, plus the serial.sh runner above. Tests use gate star test files plus roundtrip files with no generic live_test.go file and no empty files. Gates live in testbed/live/gates (6 files), per-peer checks in testbed/live/cyclone (15 files, SPDP acceptance) and testbed/live/ros (50 files, String round trip plus type matrix), with cli 3, actions 1, services 1, moved 3, and helpers 8.
- testbed/logs/: compose volume for peer logs. Restart the fleet with cd testbed && docker compose down && docker compose up -d. Never run compose up per test; bring the fleet up once and reuse it. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:444.

Run

Canonical Go gates with no shell:

  go test ./testbed/unit/... -count=1

  go test -timeout 60m ./testbed/live/... -count=1

Plain go test runs the same suites and skips without a peer; -tags live is accepted as a no-op selector.

Live runs need -timeout 60m: the default 10m package timeout fires mid-suite with the peer present. The ros package holds 204 top-level tests and QoS cases budget 30m each (see testbed/live/ros/gate_qos_full_test.go:37); raise the timeout further if the ros matrix still exceeds it.

Under a saturated daemon the 10s cleanup can time out and a failed AllocateDomainLease means rerun serially via testbed/live/serial.sh.

Per-package matrix (unit first, then live by package):

  go test ./testbed/unit/cli/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/datapath/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/negative/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/ports/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/sedp/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/unit/spdp/... -count=1

  go test ./testbed/live/gates/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/live/cyclone/... -count=1
  go test -timeout 60m ./testbed/live/ros/... -count=1
  go test ./testbed/live/cli/... -count=1

Skip-when-absent rule: every live test calls SkipIfNoPeer first and type
matrix tests also call SkipIfNoTypeInterface. A missing docker daemon, a
stopped peer, or a missing ros2 interface show type skips cleanly. Failed
wire, payload, or route asserts still fail. See
testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:444, testbed/live/helpers/live.go:326,
and testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:161.

Sentinel versus live-ID rule: header types carry the per-run live ID in
frame_id; types without a string field use a fixed sentinel and rely on
per-run topic plus domain isolation. See
testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:44 plus live frame_id at
testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:389, ID creation at
testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:131, and topic derivation at
testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:144. A missing type skips, a publish with
no route fails loudly after the local codec passes
(testbed/live/helpers/live.go:403-408), and backend errors fail
(testbed/live/helpers/live.go:379-385).

Unit is pure Go with no container. Live needs the already running weld-jazzy peer and skips otherwise. Go uses context timeouts on every docker and weld call plus volume log outputs under testbed/logs/ and per-run live IDs: no timeout binary, no mktemp. Detached peers run via docker exec -d writing to /testbed/logs/<run-id>.out (host ./testbed/logs/<run-id>.out), the host polls that file directly with no docker exec cat per poll, and cleanup kills the pidfile PID plus one scoped pkill per run. Per-run topics derive from /chatter plus the live ID (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:131, testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:144).

One-time restart after a compose or logs volume change (user restarts, tests never start containers):

  cd testbed && docker compose down && docker compose up -d

See CLI - /docs/cli for the CLI flags the checks exercise.

Domain split (see Testbed Go - /docs/testbed-go):

- 42: canonical ROS String peer (weld-jazzy distro entry, testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:38-44). Round-trip checks allocate exclusive pooled domains instead of camping on 42: forward at testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:107, reverse at testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:160.
- 48: SPDP acceptance, now on allocated exclusive domains. See testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go (announcement check at :97, pure-Go acceptance at :379, live acceptance at :421).
- 47: serial single-entrypoint live gate (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:41, LiveDomain; the pool never hands out 47). Serial file split is testbed/live/serial.sh. Gate 0 offline at testbed/live/gates/gate0_test.go:41, gate 1 at testbed/live/gates/gate1_test.go:32, gate 2 forward at testbed/live/gates/gate2_test.go:33 and reverse at testbed/live/gates/gate2_test.go:107.
- 43 plus 44: distro matrix. Humble on 43 (testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:46-52), Rolling on 44 (testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:54-60), Jazzy canonical on 42 (testbed/live/helpers/distro.go:38-44).
- 60 through 69: ephemeral isolation. ROS liveliness uses 65 through 69 (testbed/live/ros/gate_liveliness_test.go:35-39) plus per-process CLI isolation in 60 through 69, so ephemeral runs never hear pooled or fixed gate domains (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:50-53).
- 70 through 101: pooled exclusive domains for parallel live tests, allocated via testbed/live/helpers/domainpool.go (AllocateDomainLease at :196, MustAllocateDomain at :464) with per-process flock locks and per-run live IDs (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:131).

Only one run per domain and topic at a time. Every live run uses one per-run live ID for payload isolation and reuses that ID for start plus assert. See testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:131.

Residue purge: allocating a pooled domain first cleans that domain on every fleet container (testbed/live/helpers/domainpool.go:351). A ros2 daemon whose command line names the domain is killed, then every ros2 topic pub or echo whose container environ says ROS_DOMAIN_ID=<domain> is killed; each kill is verified and escalated to SIGKILL, and a survivor fails the allocation instead of handing out a dirty domain.

A leftover peer is not harmless. It joins discovery on the reused domain, so its user DATA reaches take loops and fails loudly as provisional decode errors, and even a daemon with no topics counts as a route and breaks CLI route-wait isolation. Parallel suites hold other domains, so the environ match never disturbs them. The topic command line carries no domain, which is why the check reads /proc environ instead of matching argv. Crash residue older than 15 minutes is still reaped for the same domain as a backup. SPDP dispose clears routes at once while endpoints survive a 5s SEDP grace (sedpEvictGracePeriod in internal/transports/dds/sedp.go), distinct from the 30s provisional TTL and immediate lease-expiry eviction: a re-announce cancels the grace and the sweep expires the rest.

Kill discipline: never run bare host pkill -f, because the host command line contains the pattern and matches itself. Kills run inside the container via docker exec with the pattern in an env var, and death is verified with pgrep before proceeding (testbed/live/helpers/helpers.go:695).

Gates

Canonical Go entrypoint is go test -timeout 60m ./testbed/live/... -count=1. CI plus hook stay offline and live runs are manual via serial.sh with fleet up.

- Gate 0 is offline via plain go test with no shell: port math for domains 42, 47, and 48 plus a Marshal and Parse SPDP round trip plus a launch corpus presence pin. See testbed/live/gates/gate0_test.go:41 and testbed/live/gates/gate0_test.go:150. The launch argument corpus is testbed/unit/launch/conformance_test.go:199 with fixtures such as testbed/unit/launch/shared_nodes.yaml and expected dumps such as testbed/unit/launch/shared_nav.expected.
- Gate 1 is live SPDP acceptance via direct RTPS with no trace grep: join the allocated domain SPDP multicast group, decode with ParseAnnouncement, and prove non-local receipt by GUID prefix inequality. It pins RTPS 2.1, vendor 01 10, unknown reader DATA, and zero deserialization failures. See testbed/live/gates/gate1_test.go:32 and testbed/live/cyclone/gate1_spdp_test.go:379.
- Gate 2 is the ROS String round trip with per-run live IDs and no timeout binary, no mktemp: forward (Weld echo sees the ROS talker) plus reverse (ros2 topic echo sees Weld pub), each asserting only its own run ID with context timeouts and volume log outputs polled directly from the host. See testbed/live/gates/gate2_test.go:33 and testbed/live/gates/gate2_test.go:107 plus testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:107 and testbed/live/ros/roundtrip_test.go:160. The ROS type matrix in testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:100 (cases) with tests at testbed/live/ros/gate_type_matrix_test.go:797 extends Gate 2 to Int32 plus Float64 plus Bool plus Vector3 plus PointStamped plus Temperature plus FluidPressure with the same forward plus reverse shape and ros2 interface show skip (testbed/live/helpers/live.go:326).

Cyclone SPDP and ROS String stay separate. SPDP checks assert wire fields and never assert String payloads. ROS checks assert String payloads and never parse SPDP trace. Scope is pinned in testbed/live/ros/doc.go:4-13. Full wire end state is in Conformance - /docs/conformance.

Conflict

A stale container name fails up with Conflict. The container name "/weld-rolling" is already in use. Remove it first:

  docker rm -f weld-rolling weld-humble weld-jazzy
  docker compose up -d

Teardown

  docker compose down

docker compose down --rmi all frees about 8 GB.

